  <!-- 6. CHECK UNDERSTANDING -->
  <section>
    <h2><span class="n">6</span> Check your understanding (scenarios)</h2>

    <div class="reveal">
      <p><b>Scenario 1.</b> You alt-tab away for 8 seconds, then return. The next frame's raw elapsed time
      is ~8&nbsp;s. Without the clamp, what happens to the cars and the player — and why does the clamp fix it?</p>
      <button class="btn" data-reveal>Show answer</button>
      <div class="ans">Each car would move <code>speed × 8</code> units in one step — hundreds of units, leaping
      across (and through) the map; collision, which only checks the start and end of a step, could be skipped
      entirely, so the player could tunnel through a wall. <code>std::min(0.03f, dt)</code> caps that one step
      to ~33&nbsp;ms of movement, so the world advances a normal amount and just appears to have paused.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <p><b>Scenario 2.</b> You want to add flocking birds. Which loop phases must you touch, and which stays
      exactly as-is?</p>
      <button class="btn" data-reveal>Show answer</button>
      <div class="ans">Add a <code>Birds</code> system in <code>core/</code> with a <code>birds.update(dt, …)</code>
      call in the UPDATE phase, and a <code>drawBird(…)</code> call in the RENDER phase. INPUT, TIME, and
      PRESENT are untouched — that's the payoff of a clean loop: new systems plug into two well-known slots.</div>
    </div>

    <div class="reveal">
      <p><b>Scenario 3.</b> Why is it deliberate that <code>Renderer3D</code> contains no game rules — that it
      can't, say, decide an arrest?</p>
      <button class="btn" data-reveal>Show answer</button>
      <div class="ans">Because render must be a pure read of world state. Keeping rules out of it means the
      simulation (in <code>core/</code>) is testable without a GPU, the renderer can be rewritten or replaced
      without touching gameplay, and the world advances identically whether or not anything is on screen.</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <p class="loopmotif">↺ poll input → update(dt) → render → present → repeat</p>
